    "conclusion": "The age-plus-PAM50-PC model had a slightly higher external Harrell C-index than age only, but the paired bootstrap confidence interval for the delta included zero. Time-dependent AUC intervals also include 0.5 at 12 and 36 months. This is an exploratory, transductive molecular association analysis, not evidence of a reliable clinical improvement."
